module Core

### The full, SIGN-AWARE floating-point classification — `FpClass` split by sign. This is the
### single-field state used by the `UnpackedFloat` softfloat engine in place of the old
### `sign`/`iszero`/`isinf`/`isnan` boolean quartet. Folding all of that into one `i32`-backed
### `choice` is deliberate: a struct of four separate `i1` (`Bool`) fields, when passed by value
### and spilled onto the stack, hits an aarch64 calling-convention bug (caller packs the `i1`s as
### bytes, callee reads them at 4-byte spacing) that corrupts the flags. One integer field has an
### unambiguous stack layout on every target. Pair with `is`/`when`: `if c is POSITIVE_ZERO`.
###
### Lives under `Numerics/` (not `Types/`) so it sorts ahead of `UnpackedFloat.rf` in the
### ordinal stdlib load order — the field-type must register before the record that uses it.
choice SignedFpClass
  ### Negative infinity.
  NEGATIVE_INF
  ### A finite, normal negative value.
  NEGATIVE_NORMAL
  ### A subnormal (denormalized) negative nonzero value.
  NEGATIVE_SUBNORMAL
  ### Negative zero.
  NEGATIVE_ZERO
  ### Positive zero.
  POSITIVE_ZERO
  ### A subnormal (denormalized) positive nonzero value.
  POSITIVE_SUBNORMAL
  ### A finite, normal positive value (the common case).
  POSITIVE_NORMAL
  ### Positive infinity.
  POSITIVE_INF
  ### A signaling NaN (arises only from raw bits, never from RazorForge's own arithmetic).
  SIGNALING_NOT_A_NUMBER
  ### A quiet NaN (the kind RazorForge arithmetic produces).
  QUIET_NOT_A_NUMBER

### True iff this class is negative (sign bit set). NaN is sign-agnostic, so it is not negative.
routine SignedFpClass.is_negative() -> Bool
  if me is NEGATIVE_NORMAL
    return true
  if me is NEGATIVE_SUBNORMAL
    return true
  if me is NEGATIVE_ZERO
    return true
  if me is NEGATIVE_INF
    return true
  return false

### True iff this class is ±0.
routine SignedFpClass.is_zero() -> Bool
  if me is POSITIVE_ZERO
    return true
  if me is NEGATIVE_ZERO
    return true
  return false

### True iff this class is ±infinity.
routine SignedFpClass.is_inf() -> Bool
  if me is POSITIVE_INF
    return true
  if me is NEGATIVE_INF
    return true
  return false

### True iff this class is NaN (quiet or signaling).
routine SignedFpClass.is_nan() -> Bool
  if me is QUIET_NOT_A_NUMBER
    return true
  if me is SIGNALING_NOT_A_NUMBER
    return true
  return false

### Folds the legacy (sign, zero, inf, nan) boolean quartet into a class. The softfloat engine
### never represents subnormals internally (it normalizes), so finite-nonzero is always NORMAL, and
### engine-produced NaNs are always quiet. Replaces the old free `uf_class_of` routine.
common routine SignedFpClass.from_flags(sign: Bool, iszero: Bool, isinf: Bool, isnan: Bool) -> SignedFpClass
  if isnan
    return QUIET_NOT_A_NUMBER
  if isinf
    return if sign then NEGATIVE_INF else POSITIVE_INF
  if iszero
    return if sign then NEGATIVE_ZERO else POSITIVE_ZERO
  return if sign then NEGATIVE_NORMAL else POSITIVE_NORMAL
